<title>LITHUANIA: No bids accepted in Lithuanian T-bill auction.</title>
<headline>No bids accepted in Lithuanian T-bill auction.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's treasury bill auction was undersubscribed and the finance ministry refused to accept the few bids that were made.</p>
<p>The 30 million litas issue for six-month paper attracted only 4.3 million litas worth of bids.</p>
<p>Banks bid for yields ranging from 18-20 percent, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The average yield on the last auction for six-month paper on October 15 was 12.94 percent.</p>
<p>--Riga newsroom +3717-22 66 93</p>
